      "question_text": "A particle of mass $15$ kg is stationary on a rough plane inclined at an angle of $20^{\\circ}$ to the horizontal. The coefficient of friction between the particle and the plane is $0.2$. A force of magnitude $X$ N acting parallel to a line of greatest slope of the plane is used to keep the particle in equilibrium. Show that the least possible value of $X$ is $23.1$, correct to 3 significant figures, and find the greatest possible value of $X$.",
